Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 03:14:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 106/154] feat(toast): the confirmation card gets its own
 window
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hosted on the sidebar's document, .toasts resolved top 44 right 14 against that
narrow column, so a Link copied card appeared in the SIDEBAR's upper right
rather than the window's - reported twice. No CSS could fix it: a card in the
sidebar's WebContents cannot paint outside it.

Sized to the STACK, not the window, unlike HintOverlayWidget. A toast carries a
close button, so it cannot decline the mouse the way the hint now does, and a
window-spanning surface would swallow page clicks everywhere it covered. A
widget only as large as its cards is not over the page when there are none, and
it hides when the last card leaves.

The visibility guard in OnWidgetBoundsChanged is deliberately not copied. That
guard is what left the hint at a stale rect: macOS refits the window during the
show handshake while the Views flag is still unset, so the resize is discarded.

Two things the scenario caught that review would not have. An unregistered
chrome.send is FATAL, not ignored, so the first run took the browser down with
NOTREACHED on toastReady. And the stack kept its window-corner insets inside its
own widget, which put the card at -24,44 in a 171x48 surface - on the right
surface, in the right corner, and mostly clipped. It now measures 5,0 166x48.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
